WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.337
"The Benefits and Side Effects of Ginseng"

00:00:07.337 --> 00:00:10.560
Ginseng root is
a popular herbal medicine.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:14.820
Like the word panacea,
ginseng's Latin name, Panax,

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.280
is derived from the Greek
for "cure-all."

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:22.200
It can extend the lives of fruit
flies and microscopic worms,

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.820
but not mice.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.020
What about people?

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.080
Well, there have been more than
100 clinical trials

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.060
using various
ginseng formulations,

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.580
but the results
have been underwhelming.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:34.860
A meta-analysis of randomized

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.660
double-blind
placebo-controlled trials

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.300
found ginseng did not appear
to significantly affect

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.560
the duration of illness

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:44.280
but did appear to reduce
the risk of developing

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.980
acute upper respiratory
infections in the first place.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.780
Digging deeper, however,

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:52.620
the preventive benefit appears
limited to Asian ginseng,

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:55.500
which cut infection risk in half
compared to placebo,

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.960
as opposed to American ginseng,

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.240
that only reduced risk
16 percent,

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.820
which did not reach
statistical significance.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:06.660
Asian ginseng can then be
further divided up

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:07.860
by processing method.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.680
White ginseng is
Asian ginseng root

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:12.060
that's simply been
washed and dried,

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.460
whereas red ginseng is
the same root,

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.700
but undergoes an additional step
of steaming before drying.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:21.720
Red ginseng is often used
for male erectile dysfunction.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.620
While it doesn't appear to help
with female sexual dysfunction,

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:29.160
a meta-analysis of a half dozen
randomized controlled trials

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.380
found that 4 to 12 weeks

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:34.680
of 1.8 to 3 grams a day
of Korean red ginseng

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.560
can improve erectile dysfunction
compared with placebo.

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:41.340
58 percent of men experienced an
improvement in sexual function

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.520
compared to 20 percent of men
in the placebo group.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:47.820
This may be due to an
improvement in artery function

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:50.520
demonstrated within three hours
after consumption.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.400
Of course, this is assuming

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.980
there's actually ginseng
in your "ginseng."

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:58.740
Ginseng is
a multibillion-dollar industry,

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:02.340
and as such suffers from
intentional contamination

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.200
with cheaper filler substitutes,

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.300
some of which may not be benign.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.640
If your quote-unquote
"ginseng" supplement

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:10.620
turns out to be just
powdered soybeans

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.360
then you've just
wasted your money.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.500
But, for example,

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.040
if it's been spiked with
illicit horse painkiller,

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:18.960
it's worse than a waste.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:23.820
A study of the more than 500
ginseng products

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:26.100
sold in a dozen countries
across six continents

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:29.040
found that 24 percent
were adulterated.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.280
This is consistent with
so-called "immune boosting"

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.300
supplements in general.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:38.400
A 2022 analysis found most such
products failed to match

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:39.840
what was on their labels.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:45.180
Maybe it's good there's
no ginseng in your ginseng?

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:47.460
From an oxidative
stress standpoint,

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:52.380
American, Chinese,
and Korean ginseng

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:54.780
all have been shown
to acutely protect against

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:58.320
free radical-induced DNA damage
within hours of consumption,

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.860
but one longer-term trial
raised red flags.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:04.620
Although four weeks
of Korean ginseng

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.420
reduced levels
of oxidative stress,

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:08.220
four months of American ginseng

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:10.800
(about a quarter teaspoon
a day of whole root powder)

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:13.380
caused an uptick in DNA damage.

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:16.860
Until it can be shown that
chronic intake of other ginsengs

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:18.600
aren't also DNA-damaging,

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:20.640
I'd recommend steering clear.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:24.540
Approximately 10 percent
of users suffer from

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:27.480
what's been termed
ginseng abuse syndrome,

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:29.220
which manifests
as high blood pressure,

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:31.980
nervousness, sleeplessness,
skin eruptions,

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.540
and morning diarrhea.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.440
Of course it may not actually
be from ginseng itself

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.380
but rather adulterants in some
supposed ginseng product.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.160
What if you randomize people
to ginseng that's been

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:45.660
officially authenticated?

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:48.180
In a multicenter,
double-blind, randomized,

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:49.860
placebo-controlled safety trial,

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:53.160
a thousand people were
randomized to 2 grams a day

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:55.860
of red ginseng or placebo
for six months.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:04:00.660
In the ginseng group, 345
adverse effects were recorded.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:05.400
But the placebo group
had 389 adverse events.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:08.520
Each of the top five
quote-unquote "side-effects"

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:11.400
were documented more often
in the placebo group.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:14.580
Outside of a clinical trial,
though,

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:16.260
it's hard to know
what you're going to get.

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:18.540
Aside from
the abuse syndrome symptoms,

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:21.060
there have been case reports
of manic psychosis,

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:24.540
estrogenic effects,
and increased surgical bleeding,

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:27.540
and so some recommended ginseng
should be avoided

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:29.220
in those expected
to undergo surgery,

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:32.220
those with
a predisposition to mania,

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:34.260
estrogen-dependent disease,

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:37.020
hypertension,
or hyperthyroidism.

